{"command": "cd /testbed && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\ndata = \"\"\"# Data Model: Atomic Batch Transactions for TinyDB (milestones 1-3)\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17 (updated for milestone 3)\n\n## Entities\n\n### BatchWriter (new, `tinydb/journal.py`)\nA per-database wrapper object. Fields (all private, in-memory, per-instance):\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `_db` | `TinyDB` | supplied instance; never reconfigured |\n| `_table` | `Table` | `self._db.table('_default')` - cached reference to the **same** object `TinyDB.table()` returns (observed `database.py` `_tables` cache), so handle coherence is automatic |\n| `_tokens` | `dict[str, tuple[str, list[int]]]` | R07/R08 token bookkeeping: token -> (canonical ops form, original inserted IDs). Per-instance only; never persisted; never in user documents |\n\n### Operation (input, not stored)\nA `dict`, one of two exact shapes (R01 + R04):\n\n| Field | Type | Applies to | Rules |\n|-------|------|-----------|-------|\n| `op` | `str` | both | exactly `'insert'` or `'remove'` |\n| `document` | `Mapping`, not `bool` | `op='insert'` | required; **empty dict accepted**; nested data deep-copied on insert (R03) |\n| `doc_id` | `int`, not `bool` | `op='remove'` | required; `> 0`; `bool` explicitly rejected (R04) |\n\n- Entry must be a `dict`; the outer `operations` must be a `list` (R04).\n- **Unsupported or missing fields -> `ValueError`** (R04 tightens R01; the earlier \"extra keys are ignored\" reading is superseded).\n- The writer never mutates the caller's operation dicts or list (R03).\n\n### Batch\nAn ordered `list[Operation]`.\n\n- Empty list is valid -> `apply([])` returns `[]`, no state change.\n- Applied as a unit: all effects persist, or none do (R02).\n- Output: `list[int]` of inserted document IDs in submission order; removes contribute nothing. Always a fresh list (R05b).\n\n### Document\nA JSON-like mapping stored in the default table, identified by a positive integer ID.\n\n- ID assignment: computed by the writer as `max(current keys)+1` (or 1 if empty) and advanced per insert (R05 clarification); the writer syncs `table._next_id` so ordinary `db.insert` continues the same sequence (R06). IDs are never caller-chosen.\n- Nested dicts/lists are stored as deep copies (R03).\n- Read back through the Table API as fresh `Document` objects - no aliasing.\n\n### Idempotency token (R07/R08)\n\n| Aspect | Rule |\n|--------|------|\n| Type | nonempty `str`; anything else (incl. `''`, non-str) -> `ValueError` before any mutation |\n| Scope | per `BatchWriter` instance; never shared, never persisted, never in user documents |\n| Binding | on success, token -> (canonical ops form, original inserted IDs) |\n| Replay | same token + identical ops -> fresh copy of the original IDs, zero mutations, even after direct DB writes |\n| Mismatch | same token + different ops -> `ValueError`, zero data change |\n| Failure | a failed batch stores nothing; the token remains free for retry |\n| `None` | normal operation; all token logic skipped |\n| `preview` | never records or consumes a token; keeps single-argument signature (R08) |\n\n### Default table (scope boundary)\n\n- The single table the writer touches, accessed via `db.table('_default')`.\n- Raw shape in storage: the `'_default'` entry of the whole-database state `dict[str, dict[str, Any]]` (observed `Storage.read/write`).\n- **Snapshot**: `deepcopy` of the raw `'_default'` table dict taken after validation, before any mutation; the only state kept between batch start and end.\n- Other tables: never read, written, or snapshotted.\n\n## Relationships\n\n- `BatchWriter 1--N Operation` (one batch = ordered list).\n- `Operation 1--1 Document` (insert) or `Operation 1--1 doc_id` (remove).\n- `Document N--1 Default table`.\n- `BatchWriter 1--1 TinyDB` (wraps; does not own storage lifetime).\n- `BatchWriter 1--N Token` (in-memory, per instance; token 1--1 successful batch result).\n- `Default table 1--1 Storage` (shared with all Table handles; the rollback path writes through it).\n\n## Validation Rules (spec FR-001, FR-004, FR-004a, FR-010)\n\nStructural validation of the **entire** list occurs before any mutation (R04):\n\n1. `operations` not a `list` -> `ValueError`.\n2. Entry not a `dict` -> `ValueError`.\n3. `op` not exactly `'insert'`/`'remove'` -> `ValueError`.\n4. Unsupported/missing fields (key set not exactly `{'op','document'}` / `{'op','doc_id'}`) -> `ValueError`.\n5. `document` present but not a `Mapping`, or is a `bool` -> `ValueError` (empty dict OK).\n6. `doc_id` present but `bool`, not `int`, or `<= 0` -> `ValueError`.\n7. `token` (when not `None`) not a nonempty `str` -> `ValueError` before any mutation (R07).\n8. `remove` whose `doc_id` is not present in the table at apply time -> `ValueError` (R02) and rollback.\n9. Token already bound to different operations -> `ValueError`, no data change (R07).\n\n## State Transitions (per `apply(operations, token=None)` call)\n\n```\nIDLE --token valid? (if given)--> VALIDATE (structural, whole list)\nVALIDATE --token replay hit (identical ops)--> REPLAY (return fresh copy of stored IDs; no mutation; done)\nVALIDATE --token mismatch--> ERROR (ValueError; no mutation; token unchanged)\nVALIDATE --ok--> SNAPSHOT_TAKEN --apply op i ok--> SNAPSHOT_TAKEN (i+1)\nSNAPSHOT_TAKEN --all ops ok--> COMMITTED (storage holds new state; _next_id synced; token stored if given; return inserted IDs)\nSNAPSHOT_TAKEN --any error--> ROLLBACK (storage restored; _next_id=None; clear_cache(); token NOT stored; ValueError raised)\nVALIDATE --structural error--> ERROR (ValueError; no mutation occurred; token NOT consumed)\n```\n\n- COMMITTED: inserted IDs returned in order; `table._next_id = last_inserted_id + 1` (or left `None` if no inserts) so subsequent `apply`/`db.insert` continue the sequence without reuse or rewind, even across removes (R05 clarification, R06).\n- ROLLBACK: default-table data identical to pre-batch state; `table._next_id = None` so the next insert re-derives from the restored max ID (research R1/R2); `clear_cache()` so cached queries refresh.\n- REPLAY: zero storage writes, zero cache changes, zero cursor changes.\n\n## `preview(operations)` state effect\n\nNone. Pure computation: validate (rules 1-6) + missing-ID check (rule 8) against current state, then return a **fresh** `list[int]` of the IDs the inserts would receive (`max(keys)+1 ... `). No storage write, no `_next_id` change, no token interaction (R05, R05b, R08). On error: `ValueError`, all state unchanged.\n\"\"\"\nio.open('specs/001-transactions/data-model.md','w',encoding='utf-8').write(data)\nprint('data-model.md written', len(data))\nPY", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "data-model.md written 6403\n"}